v 3
d esreg. Endogenous switching regression with heterogeneous selection on gains
d
d esreg fits the endogenous switching regression by full-information maximum
d likelihood or by a two-step estimator with the exact stacked-moment variance,
d reports ATT, ATU, ATE and the selection-on-gains parameter kappa (heterogeneous
d in the covariates on request), and comes with post-estimation commands for the
d diagnostics of the selection equation (esrdiag), the specification tests
d (esrtest: index, sufficiency, constant kappa, normality by regime, pseudo-DiD),
d the effect by quantile of the score (esrcurve), the marginal treatment effect
d (esrmte), and a reading of the results (esrreport). Survey weights, hsize(),
d clusters and survey designs are supported: the svy prefix (FIML), vce(cluster)
d and vce(svy) (two-step). When the conditional mean is not linear, the
d augmented two-step adds Hermite terms, in both regimes or in one (hermite()).
d The examples of help esreg run from their links; ssc install esreg, all (or
d net get esreg) copies their data into the current folder.
d
d Reference: Araar, A. (2026). Endogenous switching regression with heterogeneous
d selection on gains: assumptions, tests, and estimation. Zenodo,
d doi:10.5281/zenodo.22717029.
d
d KW: endogenous switching regression
d KW: selection on gains
d KW: treatment effects
d KW: marginal treatment effect
d KW: specification tests
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Version: 1.0.0
d Distribution-Date: 20261003
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar, Universite Laval and PEP
d Support: see the GitHub page
d
